1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,180
You'd never expect a map

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,682
from 1513 to show Antarctica.

3
00:00:03,702 --> 00:00:04,470
But some say this one

4
00:00:04,490 --> 00:00:06,109
does. What is it, actually?

5
00:00:06,129 --> 00:00:08,342
In the 1960s, a writer claimed its

6
00:00:08,362 --> 00:00:11,744
bottom edge was Antarctica's coast, without ice.

7
00:00:11,764 --> 00:00:14,413
But Piri Reis built it from older maps. And

8
00:00:14,433 --> 00:00:17,665
that coast fits South America, bent along the page.

9
00:00:17,685 --> 00:00:20,092
An early map of South America. Solved.

10
00:00:20,112 --> 00:00:22,782
Five more Antarctic mysteries are on the channel.
